 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Modal in the past Konjunktiv II",
     "texto": [
      "It is formed with **hätte** + infinitive of the modal + the infinitive of the main verb: **Ich hätte früher anrufen müssen** (I should have called earlier). The order sounds strange at first, because both infinitives go at the end: **hätte … anrufen müssen**.",
      "With «können» or «wollen» it is done in the same way: **Er hätte kommen können** (he could have come), **Sie hätte es wissen wollen** (she would have wanted to know it)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "With sein or gewesen",
     "texto": [
      "If the main verb is one of movement, **wäre** (sein) is used: **Wir wären gern gekommen** (we would have liked to come). This form is used for what would have been necessary and did not happen.",
      "Beware of the false friend: **müssen** in the past Konjunktiv II means «should have», not «had to»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
